IMPORT prelude

-- Planning Act 1998 (Singapore) -- what is development, what is subdivision, the duty to get permission and its
-- penalties, the owner's responsibility for a tenant, the dormitory and short-term rental rules, and the life of a
-- permission: ss 2 to 4, 12, 12A, 20 and the Fourth Schedule.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ (amendments
-- to Act 23 of 2023, Act 25 of 2024 and Act 5 of 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 46 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, most often s 5 (15, the competent
-- authority) and s 21 (9). SCOPED to development control as it meets an owner or occupier. Not encoded: the Master Plan
-- and conservation guidelines (Part 2), the application procedure in ss 12B to 19A, qualified persons (Part 3A), the
-- information and entry powers, recovery of money (Part 6) except where noted, and the transitional provisions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Planning Act 1998 -- development`

§§ `3 -- development`

-- s 3(1): "development" means "the carrying out of any building, engineering, mining, earthworks or other operations
-- in, on, over or under land, or the making of any material change in the use of any building or land".
-- s 3(2): NOT development, among others: (a) works that "do not materially affect the external appearance or the floor
-- area"; (f) incidental use within the curtilage of a dwelling house; (h) a change within the same use class.
-- s 3(3): IS development, among others: (a) using one house as two or more; (b) using as a dwelling a building not built
-- for habitation; (c) using a dwelling house for other purposes; (d) "the use for a purpose specified in the Fourth
-- Schedule of a building ... originally constructed as a dwelling house ..., WHETHER SUCH USE COMMENCED BEFORE, ON OR AFTER
-- 15 May 2017"; (e) demolition, reconstruction or addition; (f) advertising on an external part of a building not
-- normally so used.
-- Fourth Schedule: "1. Use of a dwelling house to provide dormitory accommodation. 2. Use of a dwelling house to provide
-- short-term accommodation, where the dwelling house or any part of it is occupied by the same person for a period of
-- LESS THAN 3 CONSECUTIVE MONTHS and ... provided ... in return for the payment of rent or other form of consideration".
-- s 2: "dormitory accommodation" includes accommodation occupied by 7 or more individuals for rent or consideration,
-- except where the occupants are only family (by blood, marriage or adoption), a domestic worker whose work permit gives
-- the address, and a carer.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `building an extension`
    `demolishing a building`
    `internal renovation not affecting appearance or floor area`
    `using a house as two separate houses`
    `using a house as an office`
    `using a warehouse as a dwelling`
    `a garden shed for household use`
    `changing within the same use class`
    `an advertisement on a wall not normally used for one`
    `letting a home to the same tenant for 3 months or more`
    `letting a home for paid stays of under 3 months`
    `letting a home as dormitory accommodation`
    `a family living in its own home`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is development` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `internal renovation not affecting appearance or floor area` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a garden shed for household use` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `changing within the same use class` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `letting a home to the same tenant for 3 months or more` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a family living in its own home` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (A garden shed is a building operation within s 3(1); it is shown here as not development on the footing that it is a
-- "minor work" declared under s 3(2)(b) or an incidental use under (f). That is an assumption; no declaration under
-- s 3(2)(b) was retrieved.)

-- The Fourth Schedule's short-term test.
DECLARE Stay HAS
    `in a building originally constructed as a dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months the same person occupies` IS A NUMBER
    `rent or other consideration is paid` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the stay` IS A Stay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stay is short-term accommodation under the Fourth Schedule` IF
        `the stay`'s `in a building originally constructed as a dwelling house`
    AND `the stay`'s `months the same person occupies` LESS THAN 3
    AND `the stay`'s `rent or other consideration is paid`

-- The dormitory test: 7 or more paying occupants, unless all are one family plus a domestic worker and a carer.
DECLARE Household HAS
    `paying occupants` IS A NUMBER
    `all occupants are one family, a domestic worker registered there, or a carer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the household` IS A Household
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accommodation is dormitory accommodation` IF
        `the household`'s `paying occupants` AT LEAST 7
    AND NOT `the household`'s `all occupants are one family, a domestic worker registered there, or a carer`

-- s 3(3)(d): it does not matter that the use began before 15 May 2017.
GIVEN `year the use began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `use before 2017 escapes the Fourth Schedule` IF
    FALSE

§§ `4 -- subdivision`

-- s 4(1): a person subdivides land if they dispose of part of it so that the part becomes capable of separate
-- registration. (2): leases NOT a disposal: (a), (b) up to an aggregate of 14 years for Third Schedule developments;
-- (c) for other land, "a term not exceeding an aggregate of 7 years". (4): (a) an option to extend counts towards the
-- term; (b) a break on an event does not shorten it.
GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER, `option years` IS A NUMBER, `in a Third Schedule development` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease of part is a subdivision` IF
    IF `in a Third Schedule development`
    THEN `term in years` PLUS `option years` GREATER THAN 14
    ELSE `term in years` PLUS `option years` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `12 -- permission, and the penalty for doing without`

-- s 12(1) to (3): no development without planning permission, no works in a conservation area without conservation
-- permission, no subdivision without subdivision permission -- whether the person carries it out "or permit[s]" it.
-- (4)(a): a fine up to $200,000 (and $10,000 a day continuing) -- NO imprisonment for a first offender. (4)(b): a REPEAT
-- offender, $200,000 or 12 months or both.
-- (5): demolition in a conservation area: $500,000 or 12 months.
-- (6): where the contravention "involves the use of any land or building to provide DORMITORY accommodation": $200,000 or
-- 12 months -- imprisonment available on a FIRST offence.
--
-- Short-term letting and dormitory letting are both Fourth Schedule uses of a home. A first-time dormitory operator
-- faces prison; a first-time short-term letting host faces only a fine.
DECLARE Breach HAS
    `the breach involves dormitory accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the breach includes demolition in a conservation area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the breach`'s `the breach includes demolition in a conservation area` THEN 500000 ELSE 200000

-- In months.
GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment` MEANS
    IF     `the breach`'s `the breach includes demolition in a conservation area`
        OR `the breach`'s `the breach involves dormitory accommodation`
        OR `the breach`'s `is a repeat offender`
    THEN 12
    ELSE 0

§§ `12A -- the owner and the tenant`

-- s 12A(1): "If a tenant or contractor of the owner of any land -- (a) carries out any development of the land in
-- contravention of section 12(1) ... the owner of the land is TAKEN to have permitted" it.
-- (2): the owner's defence -- proof, on the balance of probabilities, of "(a) [taking] all reasonable precautions to
-- prevent the contravention ...; or (b) [that the owner] could not, by the exercise of due diligence, have prevented" it.
-- (3): it is enough that the offence occurred when the defendant was not yet the owner and was another's act.
-- (4): the owner may be convicted whether or not the tenant is.
--
-- A tenant who sublets a flat for short stays makes the owner presumptively guilty of the $200,000 offence.
DECLARE OwnerCase HAS
    `the tenant or contractor carried out unauthorised development` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `due diligence could not have prevented it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it happened before the defendant owned the land and was another's act` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the case` IS AN OwnerCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is guilty of permitting the development` IF
        `the case`'s `the tenant or contractor carried out unauthorised development`
    AND NOT `the case`'s `the owner took all reasonable precautions`
    AND NOT `the case`'s `due diligence could not have prevented it`
    AND NOT `the case`'s `it happened before the defendant owned the land and was another's act`

GIVEN `the tenant has been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner's conviction depends on the tenant's` IF
    FALSE

§§ `20 -- permissions lapse unless COMPLETED in two years`

-- s 20(1): unless a condition says otherwise, a planning or conservation permission "lapses if the development or
-- works authorised by it are not COMPLETED or effected within 2 years of" the grant, or of the determination or
-- withdrawal of a s 22 appeal. (2): the competent authority may extend.
--
-- The test is completion, not commencement: a project begun but unfinished at two years has lost its permission unless
-- extended or conditioned otherwise. And s 3(3)(k): continuing a use after a permission for a specified period lapses is
-- itself development from the date of lapse.
DECLARE Permission HAS
    `months since grant or appeal outcome` IS A NUMBER
    `works completed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a condition provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `extended by the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the permission` IS A Permission
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permission has lapsed` IF
        `the permission`'s `months since grant or appeal outcome` AT LEAST 24
    AND NOT `the permission`'s `works completed`
    AND NOT `the permission`'s `a condition provides otherwise`
    AND NOT `the permission`'s `extended by the competent authority`
